WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:20.340
Brandi was 8 years old when her father was
taken from her and her story is not unique,

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:23.300
she's just one of the hundred thousand American
children each year

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.120
who lose at least one parent to deportation.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.920
And now she's just one of the many children
Nora Sandigo provides for.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.520
I'm the legal guardian for 817 kids.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.790
Yes, you heard her correctly, Nora Sandigo,
a Miami resident,

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:44.160
is providing for 817 US Citizen children who
have been effected by parental deportations.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:49.980
Most of my kids suffer a lot because they
don't know that if,

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:54.440
at that point of their life they can be alone

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:59.000
because the father or mother was deported
or could be deported.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.540
Family unity is a non partisan value,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.920
however, mixed status families bring a unique
twist when dealing with immigration policy.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.380
Should immigrants who have established American
families

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.220
be forgiven for their illegal entry into the
country?

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.800
President Obama says yes and has attempted
to address these issues through executive action.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:18.720
However real and lasting change must come
through Congress

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.400
and until that happens many American children
remain uncertain of their family's future.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.620
The two major principles of immigration law
are protecting American workers

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.240
but the other part is family unification.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:35.070
Ira Kurzban has been a Miami based immigration
lawyer for over 30 years.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:39.760
And what the president is doing is focusing
on that second one and saying

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.140
'if you have an American citizen child or
a lawful permanent resident child

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.600
we're gonna let you stay here and take care
of your child.'

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:52.640
That's not something that's on the government,
you are illegally here,

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:56.869
you lied repeatedly and probably committed
a whole string of other crimes

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:01.300
identity theft and what have you, perjury,
tax fraud

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:03.080
and you're now going to have to pay for that

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:06.260
not by going to jail, but just by going back home
to your own country.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.280
You can take your little kids with you.

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:12.260
But you have to bear the responsibility for
your crimes.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.760
Mark Krikorian is the director of the Center
for Immigration Studies

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.960
a think tank that argues for less immigration
altogether.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:24.180
There's nothing that prevents immigrants being
deported from taking their kids with them.

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.140
But immigration lawyers say that's not true.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:31.200
When illegal immigrants are caught, they're
often detained far from where their families live

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.920
and are physically unable to take care of
their children.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:44.220
Once the child protective services are involved

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.360
it can be very difficult for an illegal immigrant
to retain custody of their children.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.740
The question is who takes care of the child?

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.620
If the child becomes a dependent on the state

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:58.060
then the state has to find a family that will
take care of the child

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.000
just like any other American citizen.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.480
In 2011, at least 5100 children were int he
foster care system due to parental deportation.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.920
This costs the government on average about
26000 dollars a year

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.460
for every child in foster care.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.520
This means that in 2011,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:20.700
the US spent at the very least 133 million
dollars on foster care for these children.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:24.680
In more recent years, that figure may be over
600 million dollars

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.520
as the number of children is estimated to
be closer to 15000.

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:55.960
These parents have signed a contract before
their deportation

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.980
granting Nora powers of attorney over their
kids.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.120
That way if the parents are deported,

00:04:01.129 --> 00:04:03.840
Nora is there to make sure the children are
placed in good homes

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.260
with families or friends.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.820
They're using this foster care argument as
a wedge

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.300
to argue that the parents should be able to stay

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.540
but that discussion is not even appropriate
as a political discussion

00:04:15.549 --> 00:04:22.800
not because the parents of kids who were born
here shouldn't at some point get amnesty

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.660
I mean I don't like it, but you can't rewind
the video.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:33.000
The problem, the core problem to me is that
we haven't actually created the conditions

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.370
the pre-conditions for that kind of amnesty.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.960
We have such a large illegal immigrant population
because our political class

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.080
has simply refused to enforce the existing
laws.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:46.500
One law many anti-immigration advocates would
consider not enforcing, however,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.860
is the 14th Amendment.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:50.100
End automatic citizenship at birth,

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:54.020
it's not just being abused by illegal immigrants,
it's being abused by tourists,

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:57.880
foreign students have kids here, graduate
students here for a few years

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.380
and then they leave and those kids aren't
American.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.800
This conservative argument, known as the anchor
baby argument

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:09.000
rests on the idea that birthright citizenship
encourages people to come to the US illegally

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:13.600
and have children in hopes that their American
child will grant them benefits or legal status.

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:21.320
That ended in 1977, after 1977 you're child
has to be 21 years old to petition for you.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.180
So the concept of somebody coming here and
having a child

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:31.410
so the child can petition for them is ridiculous,
there's no such thing as an anchor baby anymore.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:36.500
Studies show that most illegal immigration
to the United States is driven by economic factors

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.640
not the attraction of birthright citizenship.

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:44.340
But for these mixed status families any economic
gain they might have achieved in the US

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.520
is stretched thin when deportation enters
the picture.

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.610
Statistically it's mostly the father that
gets deported

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:53.940
leaving single mothers struggling to make
ends meet.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:57.600
Nora says she can't solve all the problems
her kids face.

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.200
It is beautiful but sometimes it's so difficult.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:20.960
She has been a kind of a beacon for people
who know that she is the person here locally

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:26.340
who you can depend on and she's tried to do
as she can in the circumstances.

00:07:48.220 --> 00:07:52.340
President Obama's executive stand on deportations
is still in effect.

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.900
But even if it survives court challenges brought
forth by Republicans

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.400
it will still expire in 2016 when Obama leaves
office.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.220
In order to provide lasting relief to these
American children

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:06.660
Congress needs to enact a more humane and
comprehensive immigration policy.

